  "prompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. Asset type: one independently drawn game animation sprite, hit reaction W frame 01 of 06, 40ms timing.\nInput1 is continuity reference for this same character's accepted hit peak frame03, use its native character scale, head proportions, camera, costume and planted-foot root, but redraw the specified different pose. Input2 is same-direction idle anatomy/identity. Input3 is identity portrait. Input4 is the PRIMARY approved hand-painted Q Daoist style reference, ignore all UI.\nDraw the same boy FULL BODY facing screen-LEFT; nose and gaze clearly screen-LEFT. Independently draw west anatomy with the left arm near camera holding the scroll and right brush arm passing on the appropriate far side; never mirror the east sprite.\nPose: Initial hit preparation, before strong recoil: torso almost upright, eye narrowed but open, chin tucks, both knees just begin bending. Brush RIGHT elbow at waist, brush diagonal down-forward with tip clear of clothes; LEFT hand brings the hanging scroll slightly toward the ribs. Two spirits begin tipping backward separately. This must look distinctly earlier than the recoil-peak reference, alert and not a copied idle.\nIdentity locks: short messy brown hair with high topknot; one yin-yang hair ornament and plain teal cloth ribbon with NO tassel on ribbon; round face, golden-brown eyes, tiny jade diamond on forehead; charcoal short robe with warm-gold cloud trim, ivory lining, jade belt and yin-yang buckle. Anatomical RIGHT hand always grips ONE large black-shaft calligraphy brush, LEFT hand always holds ONE blank ivory hanging scroll with black/gold rods. Brush must have ONE teal tassel physically attached to the handle BUTT, opposite its white/black bristles; scroll has ONE lower-rod yin-yang/teal tassel. Exactly TWO separate pale-cyan ink spirits beside the scroll, never extra ornaments/limbs or spirit copies. Keep established costume pendants, don't add new ones.\nCanvas/framing: one square 1254x1254 true RGBA transparent PNG, requested native at least 1024. Same scale as input1, stable virtual ground y=1155, full shoes within canvas. Root fixed, articulate knees/shoulders/elbows/wrists, retain true body compression; no global translation, zoom, scaling, cropping, mirroring, interpolation, multi-panel sheet, shadows or scene.\nClean polished painted edges and clean alpha, no colored red/yellow/green fringe, white matte or checkerboard. No letters/runes on scroll, text, labels, speed-lines, impacts or large spell effects. Return exactly one sprite.",
